p 3: Convert the sum back to binary\n\nTo convert \\(26_{10}\\) to binary, we repeatedly divide by 2 and record the remainders:\n\n\\[\n26 \\div 2 = 13 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n13 \\div 2 = 6 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\div 2 = 3 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\div 2 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\div 2 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get:\n\n\\[\n26_{10} = 11010_2\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer in base 2 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{11010_2}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{11010_2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:166"}
